# {{CAMPAIGN_SLUG}}-pm — {{CAMPAIGN_NAME}} project-management ledger

The overseeing-manager session's repo for the {{CAMPAIGN_NAME}} campaign, spanning:
{{REPO_LIST}}. Only the manager session writes here. Worker agents receive work via
self-contained prompt files (dispatched through a lane) and, where persistent, via the target
repo's `REQUESTS.md` channel.

## Layout

| File / dir | What it is |
|---|---|
| `.pm/events.log` | **Authoritative state** — append-only event log (`bin/` reads it; humans don't) |
| `.pm/index.json` | Regenerable fold of the log (`bin/reconcile` rebuilds it) |
| `STRATEGY.md` | Path, milestones, workplan — narrative, jointly owned with the user |
| `LEDGER.md` | Numbered issues `I-###` — the human narrative of what's open/active/parked/closed |
| `DISPATCHES.md` | Numbered dispatches `D-###` (+ attempts `A-##`) — narrative of work sent out |
| `QUESTIONS.md` | Numbered questions `Q-###` and answers `A-###` |
| `CONVENTIONS.md` | The operating law: numbering, lanes + dispatch identity, model routing, prompt self-containment, request flow |
| `WORKTREES.md` | Registry of every branch/worktree across the repos, with dispositions |
| `SESSIONS.md` | herdr session registry — who is doing what |
| `TRACKER.md` | `bin/track --once`'s auto-record ledger — what it corroborated + recorded, what it surfaced for you |
| `reports/` | Numbered + versioned + dated reports `R-###_v#_YYYY-MM-DD_slug.md` |
| `prompts/` | Dispatch prompt files — self-contained, ready to hand to a lane |
| `messages/` | Follow-up instructions to an already-live session `<I-###>_<verb>_<slug>_YYYY-MM-DD.md` (verbs: go, reply, …) |
| `archive/` | Where `bin/close <I-###>` moves a closed issue's `prompts/` + `messages/` (reports stay put) |
| `bin/` | `reconcile`, `lint-prompt`, `ledger-check`, `dispatch-prep`, `record`, `close`, `track` |
{{OPTIONAL_SLOT_ROWS}}

## Operating

Resume a manager session from `RESUME.md`. The manager owns state + coordination and never
writes product code (`CONVENTIONS.md` §10).
